digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate, develop, and evaluate laser-tailored conduction-restricted nanometre polymer foils driven by high-contrast multi-petawatt femtosecond lasers as a structured-target strategy for boosting proton acceleration above present limits, while using feasibility controls and mechanism-focused analysis of hybrid radiation-pressure plus enhanced Coulomb-repulsion acceleration.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When application-driven energy needs, structured-target design evidence, feasibility controls, and a plausible mechanism align, they jointly motivate a cautious experimental plan to test a specific target-laser approach for higher proton energies."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) The need to raise proton energies beyond present limits, together with evidence that structured targets are a promising route, supports pursuing structured-target strategies for higher-energy proton acceleration."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Structured-target experiments should treat high temporal contrast and micron-level pointing stability as enabling conditions because target preservation and precise alignment are both required."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Because alignment of the focal spot onto target structures is crucial, the proposal must address pointing stability as an enabling condition."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) Evidence that rear-field modulation can improve acceleration supports focusing structured-target research on designs that control electron transport or field structure."];
  "R23" [label="(0,0,0) The structured-target justification is coherent because the goal of higher proton energy is linked to a promising structured-target route and to design-space evidence favoring transport or field control."];
  "R24" [label="(0,0,0) PIC evidence for a hybrid radiation-pressure and Coulomb-repulsion mechanism supports using mechanistic understanding to optimize and validate the laser-tailored structured-foil design."];
  "R25" [label="(0,0,0) Because possible new-regime mechanisms motivate mechanistic understanding and the proposal includes a hybrid-mechanism hypothesis, mechanism-focused study should be incorporated into the research plan."];
  "R27" [label="(0,0,0) Application needs that make higher laser-accelerated proton energy essential support pursuing strategies that raise proton energy."];
  "R28" [label="(0,0,0) Demonstrated effective structured-target designs provide context for treating structured targets as a promising direction for further proton-energy improvement."];
  "R29" [label="(0,0,0) A concrete research proposal can be formed by combining the conduction-restricted structured-foil mechanism hypothesis with explicit enabling controls for contrast, pointing, and target tailoring."];
  "R31" [label="(0,0,0) The final research plan is to develop and evaluate conduction-restricted, structured nanometre-thick polymer foils irradiated by high-contrast multi-petawatt femtosecond lasers, testing whether the hybrid radiation-pressure and enhanced Coulomb-repulsion mechanism can raise laser-driven proton energies."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) The possible emergence of novel or complex acceleration mechanisms at multi-petawatt intensities motivates mechanistic understanding to guide optimization of laser parameters and target design."];
  "nC_abd_hypothesis" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Given enhanced proton energies are pursued in multi-petawatt structured foils and knowledge about hybrid radiation-pressure plus enhanced Coulomb repulsion via conduction suppression, therefore conduction-restricted structured nanometre foils are a likely explanatory and optimizable strategy."];
  "nC_alignment" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given micron pointing is required and a rule that misalignment degrades performance, therefore excellent pointing stability is required."];
  "nC_design_space" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Given multiple structured and mass-limited cases enhance coupling or fields and a common pattern that electron or field control boosts acceleration, therefore designing targets to control electron transport or fields is a promising next step."];
  "nC_design_space2" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Given rear-field modulation examples and a common pattern that field-structure control boosts acceleration, therefore target designs controlling electron transport or fields are promising."];
  "nC_design_space3" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Given reduced-size foils enhancing TNSA via electron reflux and a common pattern that electron-transport control increases energy, therefore stronger electron-transport control strategies are promising."];
  "nC_need_and_gap_common" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Given energy is needed for applications and current experiments are limited and a common goal rule, therefore the overarching goal is to raise proton energies beyond present limits."];
  "nC_need_energy" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given applications require higher performance and a rule linking performance needs to energy, therefore increasing laser-accelerated proton energy is a key need."];
  "nC_preservation_requirements" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given preserving structures is a challenge and a rule that pre-damage removes structured benefits, therefore high temporal contrast and protection are required."];
  "nC_structured_focus_design" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given design-space evidence and a rule to orient structured-target research toward electron-transport control, therefore conduction-restricting or transport-shaping structured designs are favored."];
  "nC_structured_focus_design3" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given reduced-size foil reflux supports electron confinement and a rule that confinement implies stronger transport control strategies, therefore stronger transport-control structured targets are favored."];
  "nI_abd_knowledge" [label="(0,0,0) If suppressing cold-electron conduction strengthens Coulomb-repulsion fields and can synergize with radiation pressure, then conduction-restricted nanometre targets are a plausible cause of enhanced proton energy in the multi-petawatt regime."];
  "nI_alignment_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If the focal spot is misaligned relative to micro or nano-structures, then coupling or field formation is degraded and performance becomes non-optimal."];
  "nI_controls_common" [label="(0,0,0) If structured-target acceleration at petawatt class requires preventing pre-damage and ensuring precise alignment, then experiments must include high temporal contrast and micron-level pointing stability as enabling conditions."];
  "nI_design_case_for_structured_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If design-space evidence indicates controlling electron transport or fields matters, then structured-target research should be oriented toward designs that restrict conduction or shape transport."];
  "nI_design_space_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If multiple structured or mass-limited target concepts can enhance coupling or sheath fields, then exploring a target design that strategically controls electron transport or fields is a reasonable next step to raise proton energy."];
  "nI_design_to_structured_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If evidence suggests controlling electron transport or field structure is the common lever, then structured-target research should focus on designs that enforce such control."];
  "nI_final_root_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If the overarching goal is to raise proton energy and a specific structured, conduction-restricted nanometre-foil approach is justified, feasible, and mechanism-informed, then it should be adopted as the final research proposal."];
  "nI_finish_support_structured_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If structured-target selection is supported by gap, promise, and design-space evidence, then it forms a coherent justification component for the final proposal."];
  "nI_integrate_alignment_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If the proposed plan includes structured targets and alignment is crucial, then the proposal must address pointing stability as an enabling condition."];
  "nI_integrate_mech_to_root_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If mechanistic understanding is necessary and the proposal includes a hybrid mechanism hypothesis, then the research proposal should incorporate mechanism-focused simulation and diagnostics."];
  "nI_link_mech_understanding_to_plan_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If a hybrid mechanism is proposed, then mechanistic understanding supports optimizing and validating the chosen structured target design."];
  "nI_link_need_gap_common" [label="(0,0,0) If applications demand higher energy and current experiments fall short, then the overarching goal is to develop methods that raise proton energies beyond present limits."];
  "nI_masslimited_to_structured_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If electron reflux or confinement boosts TNSA, then designs that further restrict or shape electron transport are a logical structured-target extension at multi-petawatt class."];
  "nI_mechanism_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If the acceleration mechanism changes in a new intensity regime, then mechanistic understanding is needed to rationally optimize targets and laser settings."];
  "nI_need_energy_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If applications require higher proton penetration or diagnostic capability, then proton beam energy must be increased."];
  "nI_need_energy_support_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If applications require higher energy, then this need supports pursuing strategies that raise proton energy."];
  "nI_preserve_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If target micro or nano-structures are damaged before the main pulse, then the intended structured-target acceleration advantage is lost."];
  "nI_structured_promising_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If a class of approaches has been intensively studied and shown effective, then it is a promising basis to build further improvements on."];
  "nI_support_design_and_controls_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If a specific target-mechanism hypothesis is available and enabling controls are available, then a final concrete research proposal can be formed."];
  "nI_support_structured_rule" [label="(0,0,0) If there is a proton-energy performance gap and structured targets are a promising route, then the research should pursue structured-target strategies to raise proton energy."];
  "nS10_v" [label="(10,1,0) Modulating the rear-surface acceleration field (micro-dots/pits/coils) is another structured-target method to improve proton energy."];
  "nS13_v" [label="(13,1,0) Scheme 2 uses reduced-transverse-size foils to enhance TNSA by electron edge reflection and re-acceleration with sub-ps lasers."];
  "nS16_v" [label="(16,1,0) High temporal contrast is required because the prepulse must be below the (low) damage threshold of structured targets."];
  "nS17_v" [label="(17,1,0) Another difficulty is maintaining few-micron pointing accuracy, crucial for aligning the focal spot onto target structures."];
  "nS18_v" [label="(18,1,0) Multi-petawatt peak intensity is far higher than TW pulses, so proton acceleration may involve novel/complex mechanisms; understanding the process is critical for optimizing laser parameters and target design."];
  "nS19_v" [label="(19,1,0) Proposed/undertaken approach: use a structured nanometre-thick polymer foil driven by a multi-petawatt femtosecond laser to enhance proton acceleration."];
  "nS22_v" [label="(22,1,0) PIC indicates energetic protons arise from a hybrid of radiation pressure + Coulomb repulsion, with Coulomb repulsion enhanced when cold-electron conduction is suppressed in laser-tailored foils."];
  "nS6_v" [label="(6,1,0) Improving the energy of laser-accelerated protons is essential for key applications (dense-object radiography; deep-tumour therapy)."];
  "nS8_v" [label="(8,1,0) Structured targets have been intensively studied, with several effective designs demonstrated."];
  "nS9_v" [label="(9,1,0) Modifying the target front surface (coatings/structures) enhances laser–plasma coupling, which can increase proton energy."];
  "nI_need_energy_rule" -> "nC_need_energy" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "nS6_v" -> "nC_need_energy" [label="deduction-case"];
  "nI_preserve_rule" -> "nC_preservation_requirements" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "nS16_v" -> "nC_preservation_requirements" [label="deduction-case"];
  "nI_alignment_rule" -> "nC_alignment" [label="deduction-rule"];
